            <ArticleTitle>Chemical sympathectomy with phenol for chronic prostatic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>98-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of chronic prostatitis where conventional chemotherapy and repeated transurethral resections failed to relieve pain is described. A cutaneous uretero-entero anastomosis was performed for troublesome pain and incontinence and only a permanent sympathetic block with phenol at the level of L4 achieved complete pain relief.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
